# Property XoL v1 — test fixtures

Eight edge cases for `Screen`. Each block states the input and the verdict the
contract must produce, with its clause citations.

This file is the **fixture specification**. In an environment with the OCaml
runtime it is a clerk golden test; here it is executed by `tests/run_tests.py`
against the compiled Python backend, which asserts exactly the verdicts below.
The README says which is which.

Treaty under test: retention 5,000,000; limit 10,000,000; 2 reinstatements at
100%; period days 0–365; flood and earthquake excluded by schedule.

```catala
# Case 1 — windstorm inside the period, certified, above attachment.
# claim  {1, 12,000,000, Windstorm, day 100, certified}
# verdict Covered, clauses [Cl_4_1_PerilsInsured, Cl_8_1_LimitAndRetention]
```

```catala
# Case 2 — windstorm, certified, loss above retention + limit (capped).
# claim  {2, 60,000,000, Windstorm, day 120, certified}
# verdict Covered, cession capped at the limit
```

```catala
# Case 3 — windstorm, certified, loss below the retention.
# claim  {3, 3,000,000, Windstorm, day 150, certified}
# verdict Covered, cession zero (below attachment is not an exclusion)
```

```catala
# Case 4 — cyber.
# claim  {4, 20,000,000, Cyber, day 160, certified}
# verdict Excluded, clauses [Cl_5_1_CyberExclusion]
```

```catala
# Case 5 — war.
# claim  {5, 20,000,000, War, day 170, certified}
# verdict Excluded, clauses [Cl_5_2_WarExclusion]
```

```catala
# Case 6 — flood, excluded by the schedule.
# claim  {6, 20,000,000, Flood, day 180, certified}
# verdict Excluded, clauses [Cl_4_2_PerilExclusion]
```

```catala
# Case 7 — outside the treaty period.
# claim  {7, 20,000,000, Windstorm, day 400, certified}
# verdict Excluded, clauses [Cl_6_1_TreatyPeriod]
```

```catala
# Case 8 — uncertified loss.
# claim  {8, 20,000,000, Windstorm, day 200, uncertified}
# verdict Incomplete, clauses [Cl_7_3_Certification], pending [AdjusterCertification]
```
